  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116046",
      "title": "Understanding the Element Injector's Behavior",
      "lectureOrder": 185,
      "videoOrder": 177,
      "sourceHash": "8359682492cfa0e92333ca72da2a6227f7e61dacf041413de37823386f9da06d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.63,
          "end": 2.88,
          "en": "So you can use this element injector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.88,
          "end": 6.9,
          "en": "or register a value with that element injector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.9,
          "end": 10.47,
          "en": "of this component by adding it here to the provider's array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.47,
          "end": 14.01,
          "en": "of that component configuration object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.01,
          "end": 17.13,
          "en": "Now, there are two important things you need to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.13,
          "end": 19.95,
          "en": "and keep in mind when using this approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.95,
          "end": 23.82,
          "en": "The first important thing is that now this TasksService",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.82,
          "end": 26.91,
          "en": "is only available in the TasksComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.91,
          "end": 29.61,
          "en": "and its child Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.61,
          "end": 31.44,
          "en": "So the AppComponent, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.44,
          "end": 34.293,
          "en": "would not be able to interact with the TasksService.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.52,
          "end": 40.483,
          "en": "If I try to add the TasksService here in the AppComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.61,
          "end": 44.46,
          "en": "and I try to inject it with the inject function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.46,
          "end": 49.2,
          "en": "for example, like this, if I do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.2,
          "end": 52.08,
          "en": "you'll see the application crashes again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 52.08,
          "end": 54.72,
          "en": "with that NullInjectorError",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.72,
          "end": 58.44,
          "en": "because I'm requesting an instance of the TasksService",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.44,
          "end": 60.51,
          "en": "from inside the AppComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.51,
          "end": 63.993,
          "en": "which doesn't have a provider for the TasksService.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.58,
          "end": 69.21000000000001,
          "en": "So that's important to understand.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 69.21000000000001,
          "end": 71.78999999999999,
          "en": "But it's also important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.78999999999999,
          "end": 73.83,
          "en": "that with that element injector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 73.83,
          "end": 76.28999999999999,
          "en": "every instance of the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.28999999999999,
          "end": 79.41,
          "en": "where you provide that value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.41,
          "end": 81.09,
          "en": "that service in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.09,
          "end": 83.943,
          "en": "will get its own service instance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.02,
          "end": 87.51,
          "en": "So if in the AppComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.51,
          "end": 91.77,
          "en": "I would duplicate the usage of the TasksComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 91.77,
          "end": 96.33,
          "en": "so that I have two instances of the TasksComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.33,
          "end": 99.57,
          "en": "I would also have two totally isolated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.57,
          "end": 102.693,
          "en": "and separated instances of the TasksService.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.97999999999999,
          "end": 106.53,
          "en": "And you can see that if you save that and go back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.53,
          "end": 108.84,
          "en": "you see I have the same app twice now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 108.84,
          "end": 111.12299999999999,
          "en": "essentially, two times the TasksComponent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.02000000000001,
          "end": 116.7,
          "en": "But if I add a task here in the first TasksComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.7,
          "end": 118.68,
          "en": "it does show up here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.68,
          "end": 121.62,
          "en": "but it's not part of the second TasksComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.62,
          "end": 124.47,
          "en": "because we're operating on two independent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.47,
          "end": 125.91,
          "en": "service instances.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.91,
          "end": 128.91,
          "en": "And that's all important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.91,
          "end": 131.16,
          "en": "and keep in mind when relying",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.16,
          "end": 133.263,
          "en": "on the element injector like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.82,
          "end": 138.48,
          "en": "Therefore here, I'll actually comment out this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.48,
          "end": 140.16,
          "en": "and this import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.16,
          "end": 143.013,
          "en": "because I don't want to use the element injector here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.97,
          "end": 146.82,
          "en": "And instead I'll go back to the TasksService",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.82,
          "end": 150.09,
          "en": "and bring back this @Injectable decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 150.09,
          "end": 152.763,
          "en": "with providedIn set to root.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.6,
          "end": 155.97,
          "en": "Because with that, we'll now have one instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.97,
          "end": 158.67000000000002,
          "en": "of this service for the entire application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 158.67000000000002,
          "end": 160.2,
          "en": "we can use it everywhere,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.2,
          "end": 163.02,
          "en": "and will operate on the same instance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.02,
          "end": 165.153,
          "en": "So if I now add this task here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.68,
          "end": 168.4,
          "en": "it's part of both TasksComponents",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.47,
          "end": 173.79,
          "en": "and any updates therefore happen on both instances.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 173.79,
          "end": 176.52,
          "en": "And that's the behavior I want here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 176.52,
          "end": 178.26,
          "en": "though, I'll actually get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 178.26,
          "end": 180.9,
          "en": "of that second TasksComponent here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 180.9,
          "end": 183.63,
          "en": "because it was only there for demo purposes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 183.63,
          "end": 185.46,
          "en": "but that's the behavior I want here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.46,
          "end": 187.92,
          "en": "And that is, as I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 187.92,
          "end": 190.65,
          "en": "pretty much the behavior you probably want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 190.65,
          "end": 192.81,
          "en": "in most situations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.81,
          "end": 195.39,
          "en": "Nonetheless, it's important to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 195.39,
          "end": 198.42000000000002,
          "en": "that Angular has these different injectors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 198.42000000000002,
          "end": 202.89,
          "en": "how you can register values services with them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 202.89,
          "end": 207.89,
          "en": "and what the consequences for your Components and so on are.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 208.07999999999998,
          "end": 210.99,
          "en": "And speaking of that, I mentioned it before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 210.99,
          "end": 214.59,
          "en": "but you're also not limited to just injecting services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 214.59,
          "end": 217.47,
          "en": "into Components, you can also inject them into Directives",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 217.47,
          "end": 221.04,
          "en": "and for example, also into other services,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 221.04,
          "end": 222.873,
          "en": "which is what I want to do next.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
